---
/* The front of OmniStax: what it is, and a card for each experiment. There is
   one book so far; its card is built from the manifest so the counts stay true. */
import '../styles/global.css';
import { tree } from '../lib/content/paths';
const t = await tree();
const m = t.manifest;
const sections = m.chapters.flatMap((c) => c.sections);
const built = sections.filter((s) => s.built).length;
const chapterList = m.chapters.map((c) => `${c.id} ${c.title}`).join(' and ');
const repo = 'https://github.com/BlastWind/OmniStax';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>OmniStax</title>
<meta name="description" content="OmniStax turns open textbooks into interactive editions: the original text, with its diagrams made live and its definitions, formulas and concepts kept at hand.">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,400;0,8..60,600;1,8..60,400&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap">
<script is:inline>try{var t=localStorage.getItem('omnistax-theme');if(t==="dark"||t==="light")document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme',t)}catch(e){}</script>
</head>
<body>
<main class="front">
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">OmniStax · 万象</div>
    <h1>Open textbooks, made to be worked through.</h1>
    <p class="tagline">OmniStax is a self-hostable platform for learning science and mathematics from open textbooks. The text stays in its authors' words. Everything around it is built to keep the reader's attention on the idea at hand.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="about">
    <h2>What an OmniStax edition is</h2>
    <p>Much of the effort of reading a textbook is spent searching: a diagram sits on one page and the paragraph that explains it on the next, a symbol was defined three sections ago, and the formula that ties the chapter together is somewhere near the end. Cognitive load theory calls this extraneous load, and reducing it is what OmniStax is for.</p>
    <ul class="points">
      <li><strong>Diagrams are live.</strong> A figure that would be drawn once on paper becomes a demonstration with sliders and a clock, in two dimensions or three, placed beside the sentence that discusses it.</li>
      <li><strong>Quantities carry their colour.</strong> Each kind of physical quantity keeps one hue, in the prose, the equations and the figures, so a symbol can be recognised before it is read.</li>
      <li><strong>The chapter stays at hand.</strong> Definitions, formulas, the concept map and the contents open in panels beside the text, and any section can be opened alongside any other.</li>
      <li><strong>Exercises are tied to concepts.</strong> Each exercise names the concepts it draws on, so that what a reader has practised, and what they have not, can be seen at a glance.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>An edition is produced from a textbook published under an open licence. The concepts, the exercises and the figures are extracted and built up around the text, and the whole is compiled into a static site that any server can host.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="experiments">
    <h2>Experiments</h2>
    <p class="lead">One book so far. Each experiment is a partial edition, built section by section as the tools mature.</p>
    <a class="card" href={`/${m.id}/`} data-book={m.id}>
      <div class="eyebrow">{m.publisher}</div>
      <h3>{m.title}</h3>
      <p class="authors">{m.authors.join(', ')}</p>
      <p class="scope">Chapters {chapterList}. {built} of {sections.length} sections built.</p>
      <p class="open">Open the contents</p>
    </a>
  </section>

  <footer class="footer">
    <p>OmniStax is open source. <a href={repo}>Source on GitHub</a>.</p>
    <p>Each edition is shared under the licence of the book it was adapted from.</p>
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>

<style>
  html,body{height:auto;overflow:auto}
  .front{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:72px 40px 120px}
  .hero{margin-bottom:3rem}
  .hero h1{font-size:2.6rem;margin-top:0.4rem;max-width:18ch}
  .tagline{font-size:1.15rem;max-width:58ch;margin-top:1.2rem}
  .about h2, .experiments h2{margin-top:2.4rem;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding-top:1.2rem}
  .about p{max-width:66ch}
  .points{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.2rem 0 1.4rem}
  .points li{padding-left:18px;border-left:3px solid var(--rule);margin-bottom:0.9rem;max-width:66ch}
  .points strong{font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600}
  .experiments .lead{margin-bottom:1.2rem}
  .card{display:block;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:8px;padding:20px 24px 18px;text-decoration:none;font-family:var(--sans);max-width:460px}
  .card:hover{background:var(--soft);border-color:var(--thumb)}
  .card:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}
  .card h3{margin:4px 0 2px;font-size:1.35rem}
  .card p{margin:0}
  .card .authors{color:var(--muted);font-size:0.95rem}
  .card .scope{margin-top:12px;font-size:0.95rem}
  .card .open{margin-top:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--accent)}
  @media (max-width:900px){ .front{padding:40px 18px 80px} .hero h1{font-size:2.1rem} }
</style>
